  "stem": "A particle of mass M originally at rest is subjected to a force whose direction is constant but magnitude varies with time according to relation $F = F_{0}\\left\\lbrack 1 - \\left( \\frac{t - T}{T} \\right)^{2} \\right\\rbrack$; where $F_{0}$ and T are constants. The force acts only for a time interval 2T. The velocity v of the particle after time 2T is:",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{2F_{0}T}{M}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{F_{0}T}{2M}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{{4F}_{0}T}{3M}$",
    "D": "$\\frac{F_{0}T}{3M}$"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "C"
    ]
  },
